        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "cdb912af-f6f2-55d5-8f64-de01600610fc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Vadim Berezinskii, David J. Thouless, John M. Kosterlitz, F. Duncan M. Haldane, J. Michael Kosterlitz\n- Places: Kiev, Moscow\n- Concepts: Berezinskii–Kosterlitz–Thouless transition, topological phase transitions, topological phases of matter\n- Awards: Nobel Prize in Physics, Wolf Prize\n\nFacts:\n- Vadim L'vovich Berezinskii was born on 15 July 1935 in Kiev and died on 23 June 1980 in Moscow.\n- Vadim Berezinskii was a Soviet physicist.\n- Vadim Berezinskii's work led to the discovery of the Berezinskii–Kosterlitz–Thouless transition.\n- David J. Thouless won the Wolf Prize.\n- In 2016, John M. Kosterlitz and David J. Thouless were awarded the Nobel Prize for the Berezinskii–Kosterlitz–Thouless transition.\n- In 2016, David J. Thouless shared the Nobel Prize in Physics with F. Duncan M. Haldane and J. Michael Kosterlitz for theoretical discoveries of topological phase transitions and topological phases of matter.\n- In 2016, David J. Thouless was reported to be suffering from dementia.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
